 # Fixed Step Ray Marching
 
-Also called: Ray Marching for Volume Integration
+Also called: Ray Marching for Volume Integration, Ray-marching Volumetric Fog
 
 ## Overview
-Fixed Step Ray Marching is a direct volume rendering technique that integrates the volume rendering equation along camera rays using a constant step size, applying exponential absorption and gradient-based shading to fog-like participating media [S1, S2, unofficial]. It differs from adaptive traversal methods by uniformly sampling the ray, which simplifies implementation but requires careful tuning of step size to balance visual quality and performance [S1, S2, unofficial]. Unlike [Exponential Approximation Method](2079-exponential-approximation-method.md), which may use analytical approximations for transmittance, this method explicitly computes transmittance per step using the Beer-Lambert law [S1, S2, unofficial].
+Fixed Step Ray Marching is a direct volume rendering technique that integrates the volume rendering equation along camera rays using a constant step size, applying exponential absorption and gradient-based shading to fog-like participating media [S1, unofficial][S2]. It uniformly samples the ray, which simplifies implementation but requires tuning of `step_size` to balance visual quality and performance [S1, unofficial][S2]. Unlike [Exponential Approximation Method](2079-exponential-approximation-method.md), which may use analytical approximations for transmittance, this method explicitly computes transmittance per step using the Beer-Lambert law [S1, unofficial][S2].
 
